        "The shape of the prior distribution corresponds to the type of regularization we are applying. For example, a Laplace prior leads to L1 regularization. On the other hand, a Gaussian prior leads to L2 regularization.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Posterior Formulation\n",
        "\n",
        "The likelihood function for linear regression is given by:\n",
        "\n",
        "$\\mathcal{L}(Y|X, \\beta) = \\prod_{i=1}^{n} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi}\\sigma} \\exp\\left(-\\frac{\\epsilon_i^2}{2\\sigma^2}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi}\\sigma}\\right)^n \\exp\\left(-\\frac{1}{2\\sigma^2}\\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\epsilon_i^2\\right)$\n",
        "\n",
        "The prior distribution over the coefficients $\\beta$ can be defined as:\n",
        "\n",
        "$P(\\beta) = \\prod_{j=1}^{p} P(\\beta_j)$\n",
        "\n",
        "where $P(\\beta_j)$ is the prior distribution for each coefficient $\\beta_j$.\n",
        "\n",
        "The posterior distribution over the coefficients is then:\n",
        "\n",
        "$P(\\beta | X, Y) \\propto \\mathcal{L}(Y | X, \\beta) P(\\beta)$\n",
        "\n",
        "$=\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi}\\sigma}\\right)^n \\exp\\left(-\\frac{1}{2\\sigma^2}\\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\epsilon_i^2\\right)*\\prod_{j=1}^{p} P(\\beta_j)$\n",
        "\n",
        "Now we plug in the specific prior distributions for Lasso, Ridge, and Elastic Net to see how the posterior distribution leads to the regularization terms in the optimization problem.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Lasso\n",
        "\n",
        "Lasso corresponds to a Laplace prior distribution:\n",
        "\n",
        "$P(\\beta) = \\frac{1}{2b} \\exp\\left(-\\frac{|\\beta|}{b}\\right)$\n",
        "\n",
        "where $b$ is a scale parameter, $|\\beta|$ is the absolute value of the coefficient."
      ],
      "id": "804cbe54"
    },
